<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bracław Voivodeship</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1566–1793</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Bratslav Voivodeship</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bracław Voivodeship was a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> and, from 1569, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-of-the-kingdom-of-poland">Crown of Poland</a>, in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podolia">Podolia</a> in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. Its seat was the town of Bracław (Bratslav) on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southern-bug">Southern Bug</a>. A frontier land exposed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tatars">Tatar</a> raids and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> risings, it was annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-partition-of-poland">Second Partition</a> of 1793.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/braclaw-voivodeship.jpg" alt="Bracław Voivodeship" width="320" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Poznaniak · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RON_wojew%C3%B3dztwo_brac%C5%82awskie_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
